{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1266890-what-if-the-malhim-were-the-first-fae","id":1266890,"title":"What if the Malhim were the First Fae?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-13T00:22:14-08:00","id":1266890,"title":"What if the Malhim were the First Fae?","content":"Crazy Theory #$$<br /> <br /> So what if in Demon the Fallen the Malhim are actually the first Fae? I know people like the them being the Fera idea but I wasn\u2019t convinced or at least that wasn\u2019t the only option.<br /> <br /> So the basic idea is maybe the first Generation of Fae where the Malhim, who would be Nightmare Creatures made for War and were spirits of Primordial Fear. After they win the war they are left on the Earth, maybe stranded or maybe even AWOL or maybe meant to keep man away from the Wilderness. From these first ones ( whom we know as either the Fomorians or Winter Court) some of their children were different and represented Dreams not just of fear and horror but of other things. This is represented by the other Fae courts or the Birth of the Tuatha.<br /> <br /> Also since the Tuatha are the Children of Danaan who is a facet of Gaia maybe the Malhim then come from that Seriphim who became the Worldtree/Gaia. So that fits...<br /> <br /> Later changelings come about, and they eat Glamour like their most ancient predecessors ate Faith!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T10:44:31-08:00","id":1267005,"title":"","content":"The Fae fought the Elder Dark, which sounds awefully like the Demons.<br /> The Demons fought the Malhim, who actually sound way more powerful than the Fera could ever hope to be.<br /> <br /> Before their defeat, Demons would have been insanely powerful and probably unstoppable for the Shapechangers. The Fae were much more powerful, too, as even described in the DA:Fae book (as it is claimed multiple times in this book, that the Fae lost a lot of knowledge in their past).<br /> <br /> Have the Fae begun als Malhim? Is &quot;Malhim&quot; just a name given to beings the Demons didn't understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T06:55:22-08:00","id":1269209,"title":"","content":"I could see something where the First Fae were members of the Host who after the Time of Atrocities could only interact with humans through dreams as to obey the commandment to not reveal himself. Or that the dreams of the Host were the First Fae in the same way that the dreams of the Malfeans seems to create the entities that are revered by the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}